course: dictionary
lesson: 12210
title: Congregational
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Congregational comes from congregation, the people who gather together in a church to worship. So congregational means to do with that gathering. Look at the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «The congregational singing filled the whole church.» Here the clue is whole church. Congregational singing is when everyone in the church sings together, not only the choir. Try swapping in your meaning: "the singing of the whole gathering" still fits.
explain: Congregational can also describe a type of church. «The congregational church in our village lets its members choose their own minister.» Each local church runs itself. The clue is members choose, so the church is run by its own people.
fact: Congregation means the people who gather in a church for worship.
fact: «Congregational» means to do with a congregation.
fact: Congregational churches are Protestant churches where each local church runs itself.
fact: In a congregational church, the members choose their own minister.
fact: Congregationalists began in England and helped found New England in America, with the Pilgrims.
exercise: «The congregational singing filled the church.» What does congregational mean here? | *To do with the whole church gathering to sing | To do with a football crowd | To do with a quiet library | To do with a choir only
exercise: In a congregational church, who chooses the minister? | A computer | *The members of that local church | The government in London | A bishop in another country
exercise: Which country did Congregationalists begin in? | Australia | *England | Scotland | Wales
test: «Congregational singing» means: | the choir singing alone | silence during worship | *the whole church singing together | one person singing a solo
test: A congregational church is one where | the choir chooses the songs | nobody attends | *each local church runs itself | the government runs everything
exam: A church is congregational when | *each local church runs itself and its members choose their minister | it is always in America | it has no members | it only sings in a choir
